Z||000004||Oreif||10-29-2000||02:45 AM||||Some aftermarket brands of pick-up coils don't have the connector. (used on other GM cars with different style modules.) The instructions should have told the person to swap the connector shell. When I replaced mine last year I swapped the plastic connector. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||10-29-2000||12:12 PM||||The distributor looks like the one I replaced from my 87.  13 years of corrosion on the inside.  What a difference a new distributor made in car performance.||||reg||10
Z||000006||Jhonny||01-10-2001||02:20 AM||||<BR>I just removed the distributor cap and what a surprise ... rust, rust and more rust.<BR>I'm sure that the person who designed this won't win the Nobel prize ... ever.<BR>Can someone supply me with the GM part numbers for the pickup coil ,the ignition module and the O-ring ?<P>Thanks<P>/// Jhonny<P>------------------<BR>Jhonny Sokura<BR>Vadstena, Östergötland Sweden<BR><A HREF="http://www.vadstena.se/turism/engelsk/index.html" TARGET=_blank> Welcome to Vadstena</A><P>Pontiac Fiero GT -87 , V6 5spd||||reg||8
Z||000007||tgowens||01-10-2001||06:36 AM||||Sure, here ya go...<P>pickup coil - 10495089<BR>ignition module - 10496269<BR>O-ring - 1977935||||reg||1
